or_comm
-------

-- Unannotated multiplicative `or_elim`: the two generated minors each carry a
-- conclusion-only disjunct (`or_intro_r`'s left arm, `or_intro_l`'s right arm)
-- with no explicit binder annotation. They validate only because the parent
-- `or_elim` hands each minor a context-holey expected-conclusion hint
-- (`‹hole› ⊢ b ∨ a`) that pins the free disjunct from the concrete wff. This is
-- the compile-path round-trip of the `nd_or_comm` auto? suggestion.
l1: $ (a ∨ b) ⊢ a ∨ b $ by ax []
l2: $ a ⊢ a $ by ax []
l3: $ b ⊢ b $ by ax []
l4: $ _ ⊢ (a ∨ b) → (b ∨ a) $
  by imp_intro
  [or_elim
    [l1,
     or_intro_r [l2],
     or_intro_l [l3]]]
